---
// The privacy policy, also the App Store's privacy policy URL for the iPad app (SITE-17).
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { github } from "../site.config";
---
<Base title="Privacy policy · ViewSwitcher" description="ViewSwitcher collects nothing: no accounts, no analytics, no tracking. Your shows stay on your Mac." path="/privacy">
  <Header />
  <main id="main" class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">The short version: ViewSwitcher collects nothing. No accounts, no analytics, no ads, no tracking. Your shows stay on your Mac.</p>
    <p class="quiet">Updated 24 November 2026. This covers ViewSwitcher for Mac, ViewSwitcher for iPad and this website.</p>

    <h2>ViewSwitcher for Mac</h2>
    <p>The app runs entirely on your Mac. Your shows, views, titles and settings are saved in a folder on your Mac, and the app talks to OBS on the same Mac. When you open the switcher on a phone, a tablet or another browser, that device connects to your Mac directly; nothing passes through us. We don't run a server that your data could go to.</p>
    <p>The app goes online only for these:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Updates.</strong> It checks GitHub, where ViewSwitcher is published, for a newer version and downloads it from there. GitHub sees your IP address, as with any download (<a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement</a>).</li>
      <li><strong>Fonts in the starter views.</strong> The views ViewSwitcher starts you with load their fonts from Google Fonts when they're shown, so Google sees your IP address (<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a>). You can change a view's fonts to ones on your Mac.</li>
      <li><strong>Anything you add to a view yourself</strong>, such as an image or a web page from the internet, loads from wherever it's hosted.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>ViewSwitcher for iPad</h2>
    <p>The iPad app connects only to ViewSwitcher on your Mac: over the USB-C cable, or over a network address you type into it yourself. It doesn't collect anything or send anything anywhere else. Its App Store listing says "Data Not Collected".</p>
    <p>Apple handles buying the app. What Apple keeps about your purchase is covered by <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple's privacy policy</a>; we don't receive your name or payment details.</p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>No cookies, no analytics, no tracking scripts, and the fonts are served from this site, not a font service. The site is hosted on Vercel, which handles requests to it (including your IP address) to serve and protect the site (<a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy">Vercel's privacy policy</a>). Links to GitHub take you to GitHub.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>ViewSwitcher doesn't collect personal information from anyone, including children.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this ever changes, this page changes first, with a new date at the top.</p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>Ask on <a href={`${github}/issues`}>GitHub</a> or see <a href="/support">Support</a>.</p>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
